{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00762",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.16,
      "end_seconds": 16.94,
      "duration_seconds": 14.78,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I've been told to come back since the operation, because my stomach's been playing up. I'm trying to remember what I wanted to ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.96,
      "end_seconds": 25.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "It was your gallbladder operation, wasn't it, a month ago? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.59,
      "end_seconds": 40.9,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "That's the one. Oh, it'll come to me. The hiccups, yes! I get hiccups, and belching, after I eat. Not every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.0,
      "end_seconds": 47.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Do the hiccups go on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.25,
      "end_seconds": 59.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "10 minutes, 15 minutes. And then I belch, loudly. It's very embarrassing at the golf club."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.5,
      "end_seconds": 63.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Any vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.18,
      "end_seconds": 68.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No. No vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.28,
      "end_seconds": 77.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Let me go through your tablets with you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.87,
      "end_seconds": 100.77,
      "duration_seconds": 19.9,
      "text": "Right, I've got a list. Omeprazole, 20 mg, once a day. Ramipril, 5 mg once a day. Paracetamol, 500 mg when I need it. And, hold on, the other one, for the nerves, I think it's amitriptyline, maybe 10 mg, at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.54,
      "end_seconds": 114.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "So the amitriptyline, 10 mg, at night, as you recall it. I'll check the record. Any other medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.7,
      "end_seconds": 123.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "High blood pressure, and an irritable bowel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.04,
      "end_seconds": 129.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Let me examine your tummy. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.72,
      "end_seconds": 147.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.47,
      "end_seconds": 158.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "The scars from the keyhole operation are healing nicely, and your tummy is soft and not tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.5,
      "end_seconds": 165.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "That's a relief. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.93,
      "end_seconds": 184.64,
      "duration_seconds": 16.71,
      "text": "Hiccups and belching after a meal, in someone who's had abdominal surgery, are usually due to swallowing air, eating too fast, or acid reflux. I'd say this is most likely excess air-swallowing and reflux after the operation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.24,
      "end_seconds": 190.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Will it pass? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.62,
      "end_seconds": 204.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.17,
      "text": "Usually it does, within a few months. I'd like to arrange a blood test, to make sure everything's in order after the operation, including your liver."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.87,
      "end_seconds": 213.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Fine. Could any of my tablets be doing it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.32,
      "end_seconds": 226.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "I don't think so, but I'll look at them again when I see you next. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.67,
      "end_seconds": 235.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Do I keep taking them all in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.65,
      "end_seconds": 241.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Yes, don't change anything yet. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.02,
      "end_seconds": 246.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "And golf? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.89,
      "end_seconds": 256.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Golf is fine, just don't eat a big meal right before you play. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.75,
      "end_seconds": 268.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "Eat slowly, take smaller meals, avoid fizzy drinks and chewing gum, and sit upright for an hour after eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.63,
      "end_seconds": 274.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I like a fizzy drink. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.52,
      "end_seconds": 281.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Switch to water for a few weeks and see. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.1,
      "end_seconds": 287.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.84,
      "end_seconds": 299.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks, to see how the belching is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.93,
      "end_seconds": 306.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Four weeks. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
